/*
 * Vektorprogrammet: intended bounded contexts, context map and aggregates (Context Mapper CML).
 *
 * docs/system.md is the product authority and docs/architecture.md holds the technical boundaries.
 * This model states intent; it does not describe the code on main. docs/model/authority.als states
 * and checks the role and principal algebra that the AccessControl context publishes.
 *
 * Decisions that this model encodes:
 * - Semesters are derived from the calendar; AcademicCalendar is upstream.
 * - TeamApplications owns team intake with its own revision.
 * - Recruitment owns the onboarding invitation; Identity owns the one-time account claim.
 * - Positions are informal titles that each unit defines, kept as reference data. Each maps to exactly
 *   one role type, and authority comes only from the closed set of role types. Free-text titles are
 *   mapped once at import.
 * - Admissions owns the application's year of study.
 * - Event payloads carry identifiers plus closed non-personal values; no names, contact details or free text.
 * - A request that presents more than one credential fails, whatever their kinds.
 * - The existing-account claim uses the session as its principal; the claim token is the named
 *   requirement onboarding.claim-token, single-use and bound to its claim target. A bearer cannot
 *   make the existing-account claim.
 * - Principal-side grants and roles are independent; ending a grant removes no role authority.
 * - A department board (Styret) and the national board (Hovedstyret) are units like teams: scopes,
 *   never holders. A board role reaches its board's scope: Styret its department, Hovedstyret every
 *   department. The global-administrator grant is a separate principal-side grant for system
 *   administration; a Hovedstyret seat does not imply it.
 * - Styret holds its own positions plus one derived seat for every leader of a local team with its
 *   home in the department. Hovedstyret holds its own positions plus one derived seat for every leader
 *   of a national team. A derived seat starts and ends with the leadership and confers membership and
 *   certificate issuance, not administration.
 * - A department governs itself only while Hovedstyret recognises it as independent: at least three
 *   elected board members, and the recruitment and school coordination teams. A department that is not
 *   independent, and a team without a board, fall under Hovedstyret.
 * - Hovedstyret serves a one-year term from 1 June; with fewer than five members it is not quorate.
 * - A member is a student who holds an assistant, team or elected role; membership lapses after three
 *   semesters without a role. An active member holds a role in the current semester. Hovedstyret can
 *   grant membership for one calendar year.
 * - Leave longer than two semesters ends a team role. A new team member signs the department's team
 *   contract and a confidentiality declaration.
 * - A team has a home department and a scope: its home, or national for a national team that a
 *   department hosts.
 * - Roster member and applicant are role types.
 * - An interviewer schedules under the named requirement recruitment.interviewer-appointment.
 * - The payment destination is Economy-private data keyed by the payment-authority grant.
 * - Contact submission is anonymous and rate limited; the homepage deployment secret names no principal.
 * - School contacts are data, not principals or role holders.
 * - Only a board's leader reaches a department; an ordinary team leader acts within the team.
 * - A delegation is explicit, named and time-bounded: team T holds capability C in area A, the team's
 *   home department or, for a national team, a department or the organization. A Styret leader manages
 *   the delegations of its department's teams; Hovedstyret or a global administrator manages those of
 *   national teams. There are no roles by team kind.
 * - Every member of the national economy team approves or rejects claims through a national
 *   delegation; only its leader, the finance lead, pays out and records settlement.
 * - The global-administrator grant keeps its organisational actions for now.
 * - An OAuth client acting for a person never exceeds the person's authority and is narrowed by its
 *   token scope. A bot holds no standing capability and changes data only with the person's confirmation.
 * - Substitute coverage records absences and who covered each lesson date; coordination stays in Slack.
 * - A pure scheduling function drafts placements; Skolekoordinering adjusts the draft.
 * - Certificates are in scope: school coordination adjusts each assistant's days served at semester
 *   end, and the department's board issues the certificates; Hovedstyret's seats issue them for a
 *   department that is not independent. Surveys stay in Google Forms.
 * - A substitute is an admission outcome: an admitted applicant without a placement, on call.
 * - A Kanskje recommendation implies no admission outcome; the recruitment team decides placed,
 *   substitute or rejected.
 * - General Assembly vote weights are a derived report: active members plus 100 per department, split
 *   among its attending members, at most 25 per member.
 * - The first Google Workspace scope keeps team group membership in sync with team membership;
 *   accounts stay manual.
 *
 * Conventions used in this file:
 * - Identity value objects (XId) are declared once, in the owning context. Downstream contexts hold
 *   the identifier value as a plain attribute type (no "-" reference): they reference the published
 *   language, not the upstream entity.
 * - Authority on a write is a doc string on the operation or command:
 *   "capability: <id>; requirement: <relationship>; scope: <resolver>; decisionTime: Transaction".
 *   AccessControl owns the vocabulary; the aggregate treats the resolved actor as a guard input.
 *   Requirement words: "team.member" and "team.leader" are appointments on an ordinary team, with team
 *   reach. "board.leader covering X" is an effective board appointment whose position maps to the
 *   board-leader role type and whose board's reach covers X (a department board reaches its department,
 *   the national board every department). A department board covers its department only while the
 *   department is independent; otherwise Hovedstyret covers it. "coordinator(X)" is a board leader
 *   covering X. "department.board covering X" is any effective seat, derived seats included, on the
 *   board of an independent department that covers X.
 *   "global.administrator" is an active principal-side grant. A named requirement is written
 *   "requirement <id>"; it restricts a permit and never grants one. Where a requirement names
 *   "board.leader covering X" for a capability C, an active delegation of C whose area covers X, to a
 *   team on which the person holds a current appointment, also satisfies it.
 * - Invariants are doc strings that start with "invariant:" on the aggregate.
 * - Lifecycle enums hold persisted states only. Time-derived states (Future/Current/Ended appointment,
 *   Open/Closed intake, Overdue commitment) are policies over state and an instant, not stored states.
 *
 * Validate with Context Mapper CLI 6.12.0 (Maven Central, org.contextmapper:context-mapper-cli):
 *   cm validate -i docs/model/contexts.cml
 */

Domain Vektorprogrammet {
  domainVisionStatement = "Send volunteer university students as assistants to help pupils in regular mathematics lessons at partner primary and lower secondary schools, and run the member organization that recruits, places, schedules and supports them."

  Subdomain SchoolService {
    type = CORE_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "School demand plus eligible assistant supply becomes an automatic placement draft, coordinator-adjusted placements, a reviewed proposal, a confirmed roster, dated school-service commitments, recorded absences and coverage, one terminal outcome per commitment, immutable service history, and certificates from days served."
  }
  Subdomain VolunteerRecruitment {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Admission periods, applications, interviews, recommendations and onboarding invitations, kept as separate decisions."
  }
  Subdomain OrganizationStructure {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Departments, teams, department boards, the national board, positions and effective-dated appointments."
  }
  Subdomain PartnerSchools {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Partner-school identities, contacts, department associations and capacity plans."
  }
  Subdomain ExpenseReimbursement {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Claims with private receipt files, approval, rejection and reopening, and separately authorized settlement evidence. Approval is not proof of payment."
  }
  Subdomain TeamRecruitment {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Public applications to join one team, intake settings, staff reads and deletion."
  }
  Subdomain SchoolFeedback {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Evaluering surveys teachers, pupils, assistants and parents every semester in Google Forms. The system does not own surveys."
  }
  Subdomain CommunityLife {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Social events and team interest for student members."
  }
  Subdomain Outreach {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Mailing lists with Workspace synchronization, consented notices, reminders and digests."
  }
  Subdomain PeopleRegistry {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "The stable Person identity, its contact profile, and evidence-based reconciliation of legacy people."
  }
  Subdomain IdentityAndAccess {
    type = GENERIC_SUBDOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Authentication of people and machines, and relationship-based, time-aware, default-deny authorization."
  }
  Subdomain PublicPresence {
    type = GENERIC_SUBDOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Public content, page text, sponsor presentation and contact messages."
  }
  Subdomain DurableDelivery {
    type = GENERIC_SUBDOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Outbox envelopes committed with the business fact and delivered after commit with retry, fencing and quarantine."
  }
  Subdomain FileCustodyDomain {
    type = GENERIC_SUBDOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Private files with ownership, custody and restore."
  }
  Subdomain AcademicCalendarDomain {
    type = GENERIC_SUBDOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Semester identities derived from the calendar. Vektorprogrammet uses semesters but does not own their lifecycle."
  }
  Subdomain OperationalReporting {
    type = SUPPORTING_DOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Read models over owned facts that distinguish current from historical state and recorded decisions from inferred labels."
  }
  Subdomain LegacyMigration {
    type = GENERIC_SUBDOMAIN
    domainVisionStatement = "Temporary: evidence-based import of legacy facts and a read-only archive for the rest."
  }
}

ContextMap VektorprogrammetToBe {
  type = SYSTEM_LANDSCAPE
  state = TO_BE

  contains AccessControl, Identity, People, AcademicCalendar
  contains Organization, Schools, Admissions, Recruitment
  contains Placements, Economy, FileCustody
  contains TeamApplications, SocialEvents, Content, Contact
  contains Mailing, Messaging, Delivery, Reporting
  contains LegacySymfony, GoogleWorkspace, GoogleForms, Slack, MailProvider, HkDirCatalogue

  /* ---------------- Identity and access ---------------- */

  Identity [P]<->[P] AccessControl : IdentityAccessPartnership {
    implementationTechnology = "Identity publishes the authenticated principal and account usability; AccessControl publishes the decision language and owns the last-usable-global-administrator invariant that account disabling must respect. One transaction, one lock order (administrator set, then person)."
  }

  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Organization {
    implementationTechnology = "In-process interpreter; Organization implements the RelationshipFactPort inside the caller's transaction: a team appointment has team reach; a board appointment reaches its board's scope with the capabilities of its position's role type; a derived Styret seat follows its team leadership"
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra, CapabilityRegistry
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] People {
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Schools {
    implementationTechnology = "Scope resolver: school -> associated departments (all must be covered)"
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra, CapabilityRegistry
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Admissions {
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra, CapabilityRegistry
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Recruitment {
    implementationTechnology = "Recruitment implements the RelationshipFactPort for interview assignment (interviewer, co-interviewer); the named requirement recruitment.interviewer-appointment reads Organization's appointments"
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra, CapabilityRegistry
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Placements {
    implementationTechnology = "Placements implements the RelationshipFactPort for affiliation, placement and roster membership"
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra, CapabilityRegistry
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Economy {
    implementationTechnology = "Payment authority is an AccessControl grant; approval and settlement are national delegations to the economy team. Economy keeps the payment destination keyed by the payment-authority grant and implements the RelationshipFactPort for claim ownership"
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra, CapabilityRegistry, Grants, Delegations
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] TeamApplications {
    implementationTechnology = "Requirement team.member (read) and team.leader (change); global administration and board seats grant no implicit access"
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra, CapabilityRegistry
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] SocialEvents {
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Content {
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Mailing {
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra
  }
  AccessControl [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Reporting {
    exposedAggregates = PrincipalAlgebra
  }

  People [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Identity {
    implementationTechnology = "An Account authenticates exactly one Person; the account key is the PersonId"
    exposedAggregates = Person
  }
  People [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Organization {
    exposedAggregates = Person
  }
  People [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Recruitment {
    exposedAggregates = Person, Profile
  }
  People [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Placements {
    exposedAggregates = Person, Profile
  }
  People [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Economy {
    exposedAggregates = Person
  }
  People [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Content {
    exposedAggregates = Profile
  }
  People [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,ACL] Mailing {
    implementationTechnology = "Contact profile -> copyable recipient address; a missing contact is absent, an infrastructure failure is not an empty success"
    exposedAggregates = Profile
  }
  People [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Reporting {
    exposedAggregates = Person, Profile
  }

  /* ---------------- Reference data ---------------- */

  AcademicCalendar [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Admissions {
    exposedAggregates = SemesterCatalogue
  }
  AcademicCalendar [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Schools {
    exposedAggregates = SemesterCatalogue
  }
  AcademicCalendar [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Placements {
    exposedAggregates = SemesterCatalogue
  }
  AcademicCalendar [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] SocialEvents {
    exposedAggregates = SemesterCatalogue
  }
  AcademicCalendar [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Mailing {
    exposedAggregates = SemesterCatalogue
  }
  AcademicCalendar [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Reporting {
    exposedAggregates = SemesterCatalogue
  }

  Organization [D,ACL] <- [U,OHS,PL] HkDirCatalogue {
    implementationTechnology = "Candidate source for fields of study; not selected"
  }

  /* ---------------- Organization as upstream of scoped work ---------------- */

  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,ACL] TeamApplications {
    implementationTechnology = "Team and department activity plus mailbox, translated into TeamIntakeFacts; the intake itself is TeamApplications' own, and TeamApplications never writes Organization state"
    exposedAggregates = Team, Department
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Schools {
    exposedAggregates = Department
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Admissions {
    exposedAggregates = Department, FieldOfStudy
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Recruitment {
    exposedAggregates = Department
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Placements {
    exposedAggregates = Department
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Economy {
    exposedAggregates = Department
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] SocialEvents {
    exposedAggregates = Department
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Content {
    exposedAggregates = Department
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Contact {
    implementationTechnology = "Department mailbox and activity"
    exposedAggregates = Department
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Mailing {
    implementationTechnology = "Nonsuspended appointments overlapping a semester (touching a boundary does not qualify)"
    exposedAggregates = Appointment
  }
  Organization [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Reporting {
    implementationTechnology = "Active members per department, from current appointments; the General Assembly vote-weight report reads them"
    exposedAggregates = Department, Team, Appointment
  }

  /* ---------------- Recruitment chain ---------------- */

  Admissions [U,S] -> [D,C] Recruitment {
    implementationTechnology = "Interview assignment reads the application and its admission period"
    exposedAggregates = AdmissionApplication, AdmissionPeriod
  }
  Identity [U,S] -> [D,C] Recruitment {
    implementationTechnology = "An onboarding invitation carries an Identity claim capability; claiming links an account and grants neither affiliation nor placement"
    exposedAggregates = AccountClaim
  }
  Admissions [U,S] -> [D,C] Messaging {
    implementationTechnology = "Admission-opening notices with subscription consent"
    exposedAggregates = AdmissionPeriod
  }
  Recruitment [U,S] -> [D,C] Messaging {
    implementationTechnology = "Accept-interview reminders and staff interview digests"
    exposedAggregates = Interview
  }

  /* ---------------- School service core ---------------- */

  Schools [U,S] -> [D,C] Placements {
    implementationTechnology = "Active school, department association and capacity, which bounds the scheduling function; Placements answers the dependent-records query Schools needs before an association is removed"
    exposedAggregates = School, CapacityPlan
  }
  Admissions [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Placements {
    implementationTechnology = "The scheduling function reads each accepted applicant's weekday availability, bolk and school wishes from the application; Placements never writes them"
    exposedAggregates = AdmissionApplication
  }
  Placements [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Mailing {
    implementationTechnology = "Assistant recipients: accepted historical service and active placements for a department and semester"
    exposedAggregates = Placement, HistoricalService
  }

  /* ---------------- Economy ---------------- */

  FileCustody [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Economy {
    implementationTechnology = "Private receipt files; SQL and file storage never share a transaction"
    exposedAggregates = PrivateFile
  }

  /* ---------------- Durable delivery ---------------- */

  Delivery [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Identity {
    exposedAggregates = OutboxEnvelope
  }
  Delivery [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Admissions {
    exposedAggregates = OutboxEnvelope
  }
  Delivery [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Recruitment {
    exposedAggregates = OutboxEnvelope
  }
  Delivery [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Placements {
    exposedAggregates = OutboxEnvelope
  }
  Delivery [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Economy {
    exposedAggregates = OutboxEnvelope
  }
  Delivery [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] TeamApplications {
    exposedAggregates = OutboxEnvelope
  }
  Delivery [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Messaging {
    exposedAggregates = OutboxEnvelope
  }
  Delivery [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Contact {
    implementationTechnology = "Contact relays a transient message; the quota commits first and delivery uses the shared Mail port"
    exposedAggregates = OutboxEnvelope
  }
  Delivery [D,ACL] <- [U,OHS] MailProvider {
    implementationTechnology = "Provider Layer; a provider failure never rolls back a business fact"
  }
  Mailing [D,ACL] <- [U,OHS] GoogleWorkspace {
    implementationTechnology = "Automated synchronization; the first scope keeps team group membership, derived Styret seats included, in sync with team membership; accounts stay manual"
  }

  /* ---------------- Reporting ---------------- */

  Admissions [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Reporting {
    exposedAggregates = AdmissionApplication
  }
  Recruitment [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Reporting {
    exposedAggregates = Interview, OnboardingInvitation
  }
  Placements [U,OHS,PL] -> [D,CF] Reporting {
    implementationTechnology = "Active assistants per department and semester count as active members"
    exposedAggregates = VolunteerAffiliation, Placement, SchoolServiceCommitment
  }

  /* ---------------- Legacy migration (temporary) ---------------- */

  People [D,ACL] <- [U] LegacySymfony {
    implementationTechnology = "Explicit source-to-Person mapping with identity evidence; quarantine without partial writes"
  }
  Identity [D,ACL] <- [U] LegacySymfony {
    implementationTechnology = "Account import requires accepted Person evidence; legacy aliases never become login identities"
  }
  Organization [D,ACL] <- [U] LegacySymfony {
    implementationTechnology = "Reviewed cohort; historical membership never becomes current authority by inference"
  }
  Placements [D,ACL] <- [U] LegacySymfony {
    implementationTechnology = "Reviewed current assignments and append-only historical service"
  }
  Economy [D,ACL] <- [U] LegacySymfony {
    implementationTechnology = "Reviewed receipts; a legacy refund becomes approval, not proof of payment"
  }
  TeamApplications [D,ACL] <- [U] LegacySymfony {
    implementationTechnology = "Applications open at cutover"
  }
}

/* ======================================================================================
 * Identity and access
 * ====================================================================================== */

BoundedContext AccessControl implements IdentityAndAccess {
  type = SYSTEM
  domainVisionStatement = "Publishes the principal, scope, role, capability and decision language every context authorizes against. permit = exactly one usable principal AND (an effective role whose reach covers the resource, with its named requirements met, OR an active principal-side grant that covers it, OR an unconsumed bearer capability for exactly this resource). An OAuth client acting for a person never exceeds the person's authority and stays inside its token scope; a bot changes data only with the person's confirmation. A unit sits at one scope: an ordinary team at itself, a department board at its department, the national board at national scope. Default deny; resolved inside the committing transaction; revocation applies on the next interaction."
  responsibilities = "Principal algebra", "Role algebra", "Capability registry", "Grants", "Capability interpreter", "Relationship fact port"
  implementationTechnology = "Pure interpreter in the domain package; each fact-owning context implements the fact port in its adapter"

  "invariant: a request that presents more than one credential is denied, whatever their kinds; a requirement token is not a credential. invariant: a service principal inherits no human role. invariant: roles and principal-side grants are independent: a seat confers no grant, and ending a grant removes no role authority. invariant: system administration is permitted only through an active global-administrator grant. invariant: a delegation never carries system administration. invariant: an on-behalf request is permitted only inside the person's authority and the client's token scope; a client holds no standing capability. invariant: at least one usable global administrator exists after every committed command."
  Aggregate PrincipalAlgebra {
    responsibilities = "Who acts, under which credential, over which scope, and with what outcome"

    abstract ValueObject Principal
    ValueObject AnonymousPrincipal extends Principal
    ValueObject PersonPrincipal extends Principal {
      PersonId personId
      - OnBehalfOf onBehalfOf
    }
    "An account bearer names an OAuth client that acts for the person. The token scope narrows the person's authority; an agent client (a bot) changes data only with the person's confirmation for that request."
    ValueObject OnBehalfOf {
      String oauthClientId
      List<String> tokenScope
      boolean agent
      boolean changeConfirmed
    }
    ValueObject ServicePrincipal extends Principal {
      - ServicePrincipalId servicePrincipalId
    }
    ValueObject CapabilityHolder extends Principal {
      - BearerCapabilityId capabilityId
    }
    ValueObject ServicePrincipalId {
      String value key
    }
    ValueObject BearerCapabilityId {
      String value key
    }

    abstract ValueObject Scope
    ValueObject GlobalScope extends Scope
    ValueObject DomainScope extends Scope {
      String domainId
    }
    ValueObject DepartmentScope extends Scope {
      DepartmentId departmentId
    }
    ValueObject ResourceScope extends Scope {
      String resourceKind
      String resourceId
    }
    "invariant: recursion depth and encoded size are bounded"
    ValueObject AllOfScope extends Scope {
      - Scope left
      - Scope right
    }
    ValueObject AnyOfScope extends Scope {
      - Scope left
      - Scope right
    }

    "A role instance is (holder, role type, scope, interval, status). The holder is a Person; units are scopes, never holders. The assistants of a department in a semester are a derived cohort, not a unit."
    ValueObject RoleInstance {
      PersonId holder
      - RoleType roleType
      - Scope roleScope
      Instant startAt
      Instant endAt
      boolean suspended
    }
    enum RoleType {
      TeamMemberRole, TeamLeaderRole, BoardLeaderRole, BoardMemberRole, AssistantRole, PlacedAssistantRole, RosterMemberRole, InterviewerRole, CoInterviewerRole, ReceiptOwnerRole, ApplicantRole
    }

    abstract ValueObject Decision
    "The witness is the context's typed actor (for example TeamLeader of a team); a decider takes it as a guard input."
    ValueObject Allow extends Decision {
      String witness
    }
    ValueObject Deny extends Decision {
      - DenialReason reason
    }
    enum DenialReason {
      Unauthenticated, NotInScope, AuthorityInactive, Ambiguous, RequirementFailed
    }

    Service CapabilityInterpreter {
      "Default deny. Evaluates every applicable grant and relationship fact for one capability at the authorization instant, inside the caller's transaction."
      @Decision permit(@Principal principal, @CapabilityType capability, @Scope resource, Instant authorizationInstant) : read-only;
    }
  }

  Aggregate CapabilityRegistry {
    responsibilities = "One registry binds each command to its capability, requirement, scope resolver and decision time"

    Entity CapabilityType {
      aggregateRoot
      - CapabilityTypeId capabilityTypeId
      String owningContext
      - Requirement requirement
      - ScopeResolver scopeResolver
      - DecisionTime decisionTime
    }
    ValueObject CapabilityTypeId {
      String value key
    }
    "Named requirements restrict a permit and never grant one: onboarding.claim-token (a usable claim capability bound to the claim target), recruitment.interviewer-appointment (an effective appointment in the interview's department), recruitment.correction-window (the scoped correction capability is active), onbehalf.change-confirmation (a bot's change carries the person's confirmation)."
    ValueObject Requirement {
      String requirementId
      String relationship
    }
    ValueObject ScopeResolver {
      String scopeResolverId
      String resourceKind
    }
    enum DecisionTime {
      Transaction, SnapshotRead
    }
  }

  "invariant: a grant interval is half-open and startAt < endAt when endAt is present. invariant: grants of one capability to one subject over one area do not overlap. invariant: ending and revoking have one meaning for every grant kind. invariant: a grant carries no private data."
  Aggregate Grants {
    responsibilities = "Explicit, time-bound authority: global administration (system administration, with a one-time bootstrap grant at cutover), payment authority, service-principal grants and delegated rules. Receipt approval and settlement are delegations to the economy team, not grants. No role implies a grant. The global-administrator grant keeps its organisational actions for now."

    Entity Grant {
      aggregateRoot
      - GrantId grantId
      - Principal subject
      - CapabilityType capability
      - Scope grantScope
      Instant startAt
      Instant endAt
      int revision
      - GrantLifecycle lifecycle

      "capability: access.grants.manage; requirement: global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void issueGrant(@Principal subject, @CapabilityType capability, @Scope grantScope, Instant startAt) : write [ -> ActiveGrant ];
      "capability: access.grants.manage; requirement: global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction. Ending the last usable global administrator grant fails without changes."
      def void endGrant(Instant endAt, int expectedRevision) : write [ ActiveGrant -> EndedGrant* ];
    }
    ValueObject GrantId {
      String value key
    }
    enum GrantLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ActiveGrant, EndedGrant
    }
  }

  "A delegation is explicit, named and time-bounded: team T holds capability C in area A. The area is the team's home department or, for a national team, a department or the whole organization. While it is active, it gives C in A to the current members of T. invariant: the interval is half-open. invariant: the area lies inside the team's scope. invariant: a delegation carries department administration, receipt approval or receipt settlement, never system administration or delegation management. invariant: ending a delegation removes only the authority that it gave. invariant: a delegation reaches every current member of the team, or only its current leaders; a settlement delegation reaches the leaders only. There are no roles by team kind."
  Aggregate Delegations {
    Entity Delegation {
      aggregateRoot
      - DelegationId delegationId
      String name
      TeamId delegatedTeam
      - CapabilityType capability
      - Scope area
      - DelegationHolders holders
      Instant startAt
      Instant endAt
      int revision
      - DelegationLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: access.delegations.manage; requirement: board.leader covering the team's scope OR global.administrator; scope: delegated-team-scope; decisionTime: Transaction. A Styret leader manages the delegations of its department's teams. A national team's scope is national, so Hovedstyret or a global administrator manages its delegations."
      def void issueDelegation(String name, TeamId delegatedTeam, @CapabilityType capability, @Scope area, @DelegationHolders holders, Instant startAt) : write [ -> ActiveDelegation ];
      "capability: access.delegations.manage; requirement: board.leader covering the team's scope OR global.administrator; scope: delegated-team-scope; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void endDelegation(Instant endAt, int expectedRevision) : write [ ActiveDelegation -> EndedDelegation* ];
    }
    ValueObject DelegationId {
      String value key
    }
    enum DelegationHolders {
      AllMembers, LeadersOnly
    }
    enum DelegationLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ActiveDelegation, EndedDelegation
    }
  }

  Service RelationshipFactPort {
    "Implemented by each fact-owning context inside the caller's transaction: Organization (team member, team leader, board leader and board member by the position's role type, and derived board seats), Recruitment (interviewer, co-interviewer), Economy (receipt owner), Placements (affiliation, placement, roster member) and Admissions (applicant, through the applicant link). Delegations reach the current members of the named team through Organization's appointments. Each owner normalizes its status to an interval and a status. School contacts are data and hold no role."
    boolean relationshipIsActive(PersonId person, @ResourceScope resource, Instant instant) : read-only;
    boolean relationshipCovers(PersonId person, @Scope grantScope, Instant instant) : read-only;
  }
}

BoundedContext Identity implements IdentityAndAccess {
  type = SYSTEM
  domainVisionStatement = "Authenticates people and machines. An Account authenticates exactly one Person; credentials, sessions, recovery and claim capabilities belong to the account lifecycle. A service caller is a separate principal, never a synthetic Person."
  responsibilities = "Accounts", "Credentials", "Sessions", "Password recovery", "Account claim capability", "Machine credentials", "Security audit"
  implementationTechnology = "Better Auth behind an anti-corruption adapter; the auth schema is written and read by this context only"

  "invariant: disabling access blocks native sessions, human OAuth access and recovery. invariant: re-enabling requires fresh authentication and revives no session, recovery token or human OAuth credential. invariant: self-offboarding fails."
  Aggregate Account {
    Entity Account {
      aggregateRoot
      PersonId personId
      - Credential credential
      int accessRevision
      - AccountAccess access

      "capability: identity.account-access.manage; requirement: global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void disableAccess(PersonId actorPersonId, int expectedRevision) : write [ Enabled -> Disabled ];
      "capability: identity.account-access.manage; requirement: global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void enableAccess(PersonId actorPersonId, int expectedRevision) : write [ Disabled -> Enabled ];
      "An upgrade requires the stored credential to equal the one authentication verified; a concurrent reset or upgrade wins."
      def void upgradeCredential(@Credential verified, @Credential replacement) : write;
    }
    ValueObject Credential {
      - CredentialFormat format
      String encodedHash
    }
    enum CredentialFormat {
      Argon2id, NativeScrypt, LegacyBcrypt
    }
    enum AccountAccess {
      aggregateLifecycle
      Enabled, Disabled
    }
  }

  Aggregate Session {
    Entity HumanSession {
      aggregateRoot
      - SessionId sessionId
      PersonId personId
      int accessRevisionAtIssue
      Instant expiresAt
      - SessionLifecycle lifecycle
      def void issueSession(PersonId personId) : write [ -> ActiveSession ];
      def void revokeSession() : write [ ActiveSession -> RevokedSession* ];
    }
    ValueObject SessionId {
      String value key
    }
    enum SessionLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ActiveSession, RevokedSession
    }
  }

  Aggregate PasswordRecovery {
    Entity RecoveryRequest {
      aggregateRoot
      - RecoveryRequestId recoveryRequestId
      PersonId personId
      String tokenDigest
      - RecoveryLifecycle lifecycle
      def void requestRecovery(ContactEmail canonicalEmail) : write [ -> RecoveryRequested ];
      "Recovery replaces a retained legacy hash and revokes older sessions."
      def void completeRecovery(String token, String newPassword) : write [ RecoveryRequested -> RecoveryCompleted* ];
      def void quarantineRecovery() : write [ RecoveryRequested -> RecoveryQuarantined* ];
    }
    ValueObject RecoveryRequestId {
      String value key
    }
    enum RecoveryLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      RecoveryRequested, RecoveryCompleted, RecoveryQuarantined
    }
  }

  "Identity owns the one-time account claim; Recruitment owns the onboarding invitation that requests it. invariant: a consumed claim capability cannot be used again. invariant: claiming links an account without changing its email and grants neither affiliation nor placement. In new-account mode the token holder is the principal; in existing-account mode the session's account is the principal and the token is the named requirement onboarding.claim-token. A bearer cannot make the existing-account claim."
  Aggregate AccountClaim {
    Entity ClaimCapability {
      aggregateRoot
      - ClaimCapabilityId claimCapabilityId
      PersonId personId
      String capabilityDigest
      - ClaimLifecycle lifecycle
      def void issueClaim(PersonId personId) : write [ -> ClaimIssued ];
      "capability: onboarding.claim; principal: the bearer capability; scope: its claim target; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void claimNewAccount(String capability) : write [ ClaimIssued -> Claimed* ];
      "capability: onboarding.claim; principal: the session's account; requirement onboarding.claim-token (single-use, bound to its claim target); decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void claimForExistingAccount(PersonId sessionPerson, String capability) : write [ ClaimIssued -> Claimed* ];
      def void revokeClaim() : write [ ClaimIssued -> ClaimRevoked* ];
    }
    ValueObject ClaimCapabilityId {
      String value key
    }
    enum ClaimLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ClaimIssued, Claimed, ClaimRevoked
    }
  }

  "invariant: a client holds no standing capability of its own. A delegated client and an agent client act only for the account's person, inside the token scope that the person approved; an agent client changes data only with the person's confirmation. A service client authenticates a service principal, which holds its own grants."
  Aggregate MachineCredential {
    Entity OAuthClient {
      aggregateRoot
      - OAuthClientId oauthClientId
      - ClientKind kind
      String servicePrincipalId
      - MachineCredentialLifecycle lifecycle
      def void registerClient(@ClientKind kind, String servicePrincipalId) : write [ -> ClientActive ];
      def void revokeClient() : write [ ClientActive -> ClientRevoked* ];
    }
    ValueObject OAuthClientId {
      String value key
    }
    enum ClientKind {
      DelegatedClient, AgentClient, ServiceClient
    }
    enum MachineCredentialLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ClientActive, ClientRevoked
    }
  }

  Aggregate SecurityAudit {
    "Append-only, closed kinds and outcome codes, no secrets."
    DomainEvent IdentitySecurityEvent {
      PersonId personId
      String eventKind
      String outcomeCode
      Instant occurredAt
    }
  }

  Application IdentityApplication {
    "capability: identity.account-access.manage; requirement: global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction"
    Command ChangeAccountAccess {
      String commandId
      PersonId personId
      int expectedRevision
      boolean disabled
    }
    DomainEvent AccountAccessDisabled {
      PersonId personId
      int accessRevision
    }
    DomainEvent AccountAccessEnabled {
      PersonId personId
      int accessRevision
    }
    Flow AccountAccessFlow {
      command ChangeAccountAccess [ initiated by "Global administrator" ] delegates to Account [ Enabled -> Disabled ] emits event AccountAccessDisabled
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext People implements PeopleRegistry {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Owns the stable human identity and its contact profile. Legacy data must resolve to a Person through explicit mapping and identity evidence before credentials, affiliations, placements or history can reference it."
  responsibilities = "Person", "Profile", "Person reconciliation"

  Aggregate Person {
    Entity Person {
      aggregateRoot
      - PersonId personId
      - PersonLifecycle lifecycle
      "Creating a Person writes the initial name and contact profile."
      def void establishPerson(@PersonName name, @ContactPoint contact) : write [ -> Established ];
    }
    ValueObject PersonId {
      String value key
    }
    enum PersonLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      Established
    }
  }

  Aggregate Profile {
    Entity Profile {
      aggregateRoot
      PersonId personId
      - PersonName name
      - ContactPoint contact
      int nameRevision
      int contactRevision
      "capability: profile.own.revise; requirement: self; scope: own person; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void reviseOwnProfile(@PersonName name, @ContactPoint contact, int expectedNameRevision, int expectedContactRevision) : write;
    }
    ValueObject PersonName {
      String firstName
      String lastName
    }
    ValueObject ContactPoint {
      ContactEmail emailAddress
      String phone
    }
  }

  "invariant: linking an existing Person never overwrites native profile facts and requires the expected profile revisions. invariant: inactive, ambiguous, stale, conflicting or unattested mappings are quarantined without partial Person writes."
  Aggregate PersonReconciliation {
    Entity SourcePersonMapping {
      aggregateRoot
      String sourceRepository
      String sourceUserId
      PersonId targetPerson
      String evidenceDigest
      - MappingDisposition disposition
      def void acceptMapping(PersonId targetPerson, String evidenceDigest) : write [ -> MappingAccepted* ];
      def void quarantineMapping(String reason) : write [ -> MappingQuarantined* ];
    }
    enum MappingDisposition {
      aggregateLifecycle
      MappingAccepted, MappingQuarantined
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext AcademicCalendar implements AcademicCalendarDomain {
  type = SYSTEM
  domainVisionStatement = "Identifies semesters. Vektorprogrammet uses semesters but does not own their lifecycle; future semesters are derived from the calendar with no manual step."
  responsibilities = "Semester references"

  Aggregate SemesterCatalogue {
    ValueObject SemesterRef {
      - SemesterId semesterId
      - Term term
      int year
      Instant startsAt
      Instant endsAt
    }
    ValueObject SemesterId {
      String value key
    }
    enum Term {
      Spring, Autumn
    }
    Service SemesterCalendar {
      "Total and pure: every instant lies in exactly one semester."
      @SemesterRef semesterAt(Instant instant) : read-only;
      @SemesterRef semesterOf(@Term term, int year) : read-only;
    }
  }
}

/* ======================================================================================
 * Organization and reference contexts
 * ====================================================================================== */

BoundedContext Organization implements OrganizationStructure {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Local departments, teams with a home department and a scope, department boards (Styret), the national board (Hovedstyret), positions and effective-dated appointments. Units are scopes, never holders: an ordinary team sits at its own scope, a department board at its department, the national board at national scope. Appointments are relationship facts that AccessControl reads. A position is an informal title that its unit defines; it maps to exactly one role type, and authority comes only from the role type, with the unit's reach. A title is never authority. Styret holds its own positions plus one derived seat for every leader of a local team with its home in the department; Hovedstyret holds its own positions plus one derived seat for every leader of a national team. A department governs itself only while Hovedstyret recognises it as independent; a department that is not independent, and a team without a board, fall under Hovedstyret. Members are students with a role; membership lapses after three semesters without one. A Hovedstyret seat does not make a person a global administrator. An ordinary team leader acts within the team. A functional team is an ordinary team; its department or national work comes only from delegations."
  responsibilities = "Departments", "Department independence", "Teams", "Department boards", "National board", "Positions", "Appointments", "Joining agreements", "Membership", "Fields of study", "Team interest"

  "invariant: a department is independent only while it has at least three elected board members and at least the recruitment (Rekruttering) and school coordination (Skolekoordinering) teams; Hovedstyret decides the status. A department that is not independent falls under Hovedstyret: its board, if any, governs nothing. Hovedstyret may appoint a local board when none is elected, and may dismiss one."
  Aggregate Department {
    Entity Department {
      aggregateRoot
      - DepartmentId departmentId
      String name
      ContactEmail mailbox
      boolean independent
      int revision
      - DepartmentLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: organization.departments.recognise; requirement: board.leader covering every department (Hovedstyret) OR global.administrator; scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void recogniseIndependence(int expectedRevision) : write [ DepartmentActive -> DepartmentActive ];
      def void withdrawIndependence(int expectedRevision) : write [ DepartmentActive -> DepartmentActive ];
      def void createDepartment(String name, ContactEmail mailbox) : write [ -> DepartmentActive ];
      def void reviseDepartment(String name, ContactEmail mailbox, int expectedRevision) : write [ DepartmentActive -> DepartmentActive ];
      def void deactivateDepartment(int expectedRevision) : write [ DepartmentActive -> DepartmentInactive ];
      def void reactivateDepartment(int expectedRevision) : write [ DepartmentInactive -> DepartmentActive ];
    }
    ValueObject DepartmentId {
      String value key
    }
    enum DepartmentLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      DepartmentActive, DepartmentInactive
    }
  }

  "invariant: a department has at most one department board (Styret). A department board sits at its department's scope; an ordinary team sits at its own scope. invariant: a team has a home department and a scope; the scope is the home, or national for a national team (economy, IT, expansion) that its home hosts. The scope bounds the team's delegations. A local team's leader sits on the home department's board; a national team sits under Hovedstyret, and its leader sits on Hovedstyret. The governing board creates, defines and dissolves a team: the board of an independent home department for a local team, Hovedstyret otherwise. The kind is not a role: there are no roles by team kind."
  Aggregate Team {
    Entity Team {
      aggregateRoot
      - TeamId teamId
      DepartmentId homeDepartment
      String name
      ContactEmail mailbox
      - TeamKind kind
      - TeamScope teamScope
      int revision
      - TeamLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: organization.teams.manage; requirement: board.leader covering the team's scope OR global.administrator; scope: team-scope; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void createTeam(DepartmentId homeDepartment, String name, @TeamScope teamScope) : write [ -> TeamActive ];
      def void reviseTeam(String name, ContactEmail mailbox, int expectedRevision) : write [ TeamActive -> TeamActive ];
      def void deactivateTeam(int expectedRevision) : write [ TeamActive -> TeamInactive ];
    }
    ValueObject TeamId {
      String value key
    }
    enum TeamLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      TeamActive, TeamInactive
    }
    enum TeamKind {
      OrdinaryTeam, DepartmentBoard
    }
    enum TeamScope {
      HomeDepartmentScope, NationalScope
    }
  }

  "invariant: exactly one national board exists, Hovedstyret, established once at cutover. It sits at national scope, which covers every department. invariant: its members are its own positions, such as the leader, the deputy and a mentor without a vote, plus one derived seat for every leader of a national team, such as Økonomi, Ekspansjon and IT. invariant: an elected term runs one year from 1 June. With fewer than five voting members the board is not quorate; in a tie the leader's vote counts double."
  Aggregate NationalBoard {
    Entity NationalBoard {
      aggregateRoot
      - NationalBoardId nationalBoardId
      String name
      "capability: organization.boards.create; requirement: global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction. A one-time bootstrap: it fails when the national board exists."
      def void createNationalBoard(String name) : write;
    }
    ValueObject NationalBoardId {
      String value key
    }
  }

  "Positions are informal titles that each unit defines (leder, nestleder, sekretaer, ...), kept as reference data. Each position maps to exactly one role type: team member or team leader on a team, board leader or board member on a board. Authority comes only from the role type; a title is never authority. Existing free-text titles are mapped once to positions at import. Positions can be revised and deactivated."
  Aggregate Position {
    Entity Position {
      aggregateRoot
      - PositionId positionId
      - AppointmentUnit unit
      String title
      - PositionRoleType roleType
      int revision
      - PositionLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: organization.positions.manage; requirement: team.leader of the unit OR board.leader covering the unit OR global.administrator; scope: position-unit; decisionTime: Transaction. A team leader defines member and leader positions of the team only."
      def void definePosition(@AppointmentUnit unit, String title, @PositionRoleType roleType) : write [ -> PositionActive ];
      def void revisePosition(String title, int expectedRevision) : write [ PositionActive -> PositionActive ];
      def void deactivatePosition(int expectedRevision) : write [ PositionActive -> PositionInactive ];
      "capability: access.position-role-types.manage; requirement: global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction. Mapping a board position to the board-leader role type, or changing the role type of any position in use, changes authority."
      def void remapRoleType(@PositionRoleType roleType, int expectedRevision) : write [ PositionActive -> PositionActive ];
    }
    ValueObject PositionId {
      String value key
    }
    "The appointment role types of AccessControl's published language."
    enum PositionRoleType {
      TeamMemberType, TeamLeaderType, BoardLeaderType, BoardMemberType
    }
    enum PositionLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      PositionActive, PositionInactive
    }
  }

  "invariant: endAt is absent or startAt < endAt. invariant: an appointment carries no leadership flag: its authority is its position's role type, with its unit's reach. invariant: a derived board seat is not stored; it starts and ends with its team leadership and confers membership and certificate issuance, not administration. invariant: a team member with at least one semester of service may take leave; leave longer than two semesters ends the team role. invariant: ending or suspending one appointment changes no other appointment, affiliation or placement. Temporal state Future/Current/Ended is derived from the interval at the authorization instant."
  Aggregate Appointment {
    Entity Appointment {
      aggregateRoot
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
      PersonId personId
      - AppointmentUnit unit
      PositionId position
      Instant startAt
      Instant endAt
      int revision
      - AppointmentLifecycle lifecycle

      "capability: organization.appointments.manage; requirement: team.leader of the unit OR board.leader covering the unit OR global.administrator; scope: appointment-unit; decisionTime: Transaction. A team decides its members collectively; the team leader authorizes the appointment. A new team member signs the department's team contract and the confidentiality declaration."
      def void appoint(PersonId personId, @AppointmentUnit unit, PositionId position, Instant startAt) : write [ -> AppointmentActive ];
      "capability: organization.appointments.manage; requirement: team.leader of the unit OR board.leader covering the unit OR global.administrator; scope: appointment; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void reviseAppointment(PositionId position, Instant startAt, Instant endAt, int expectedRevision) : write [ AppointmentActive -> AppointmentActive ];
      def void suspendAppointment(int expectedRevision) : write [ AppointmentActive -> AppointmentSuspended ];
      def void reinstateAppointment(int expectedRevision) : write [ AppointmentSuspended -> AppointmentActive ];
      "capability: organization.appointments.leave; requirement: self (the member) OR team.leader of the unit; scope: appointment; decisionTime: Transaction. Leave that passes two semesters ends the appointment."
      def void takeLeave(int expectedRevision) : write [ AppointmentActive -> AppointmentOnLeave ];
      def void returnFromLeave(int expectedRevision) : write [ AppointmentOnLeave -> AppointmentActive ];
      "A leadership handover can appoint the successor before the predecessor leaves; the end of the last leadership appointment revokes only its scope."
      def void endAppointment(Instant endAt, int expectedRevision) : write [ AppointmentActive, AppointmentSuspended, AppointmentOnLeave -> AppointmentEnded* ];
    }
    ValueObject AppointmentId {
      String value key
    }
    abstract ValueObject AppointmentUnit
    ValueObject TeamUnit extends AppointmentUnit {
      TeamId teamId
    }
    ValueObject NationalBoardUnit extends AppointmentUnit {
      NationalBoardId nationalBoardId
    }
    enum AppointmentLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      AppointmentActive, AppointmentSuspended, AppointmentOnLeave, AppointmentEnded
    }
  }

  "invariant: a person joining a team signs the department's current team contract, which includes the attendance requirement, and the confidentiality declaration; each signature records the document version."
  Aggregate JoiningAgreement {
    Entity SignedAgreement {
      aggregateRoot
      PersonId personId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      - AgreementKind kind
      String documentVersion
      Instant signedAt
      "capability: self; the signer is the joining member"
      def void sign(DepartmentId departmentId, @AgreementKind kind, String documentVersion) : write;
    }
    enum AgreementKind {
      TeamContract, ConfidentialityDeclaration
    }
  }

  "invariant: Hovedstyret grants a membership for one calendar year; it gives no role and no authority."
  Aggregate GrantedMembership {
    Entity MembershipGrant {
      aggregateRoot
      PersonId personId
      int calendarYear
      "capability: organization.membership.grant; requirement: board.leader covering every department (Hovedstyret) OR global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void grantMembership(PersonId personId, int calendarYear) : write;
    }
  }

  Aggregate FieldOfStudy {
    Entity FieldOfStudy {
      aggregateRoot
      - FieldOfStudyId fieldOfStudyId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      String name
      boolean active
      def void defineFieldOfStudy(DepartmentId departmentId, String name) : write;
      def void reviseFieldOfStudy(String name, boolean active, int expectedRevision) : write;
    }
    ValueObject FieldOfStudyId {
      String value key
    }
  }

  Aggregate TeamInterest {
    Entity TeamInterestRegistration {
      aggregateRoot
      int registrationNumber
      TeamId teamId
      ContactEmail submitterEmail
      def void registerInterest(TeamId teamId, ContactEmail submitterEmail) : write;
    }
  }

  Application OrganizationApplication {
    "capability: organization.appointments.manage; requirement: team.leader of the unit OR board.leader covering the unit OR global.administrator; scope: appointment-unit; decisionTime: Transaction"
    Command Appoint {
      String commandId
      PersonId personId
      - AppointmentUnit unit
      PositionId position
      Instant startAt
      Instant endAt
    }
    Command ReviseAppointment {
      String commandId
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
      int expectedRevision
    }
    Command EndAppointment {
      String commandId
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
      int expectedRevision
      Instant endAt
    }
    Command SuspendAppointment {
      String commandId
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
      int expectedRevision
    }
    Command ReinstateAppointment {
      String commandId
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
      int expectedRevision
    }
    "capability: organization.boards.create; requirement: global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction"
    Command CreateNationalBoard {
      String commandId
    }

    // Event payloads carry identifiers and closed non-personal values only (operator decision 2026-09-25); names, reasons and free text stay in projections or private annotations.
    DomainEvent AppointmentMade {
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
      PersonId personId
      - AppointmentUnit unit
      PositionId position
      Instant startAt
      Instant endAt
    }
    DomainEvent AppointmentRevised {
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
      PositionId position
      Instant startAt
      Instant endAt
    }
    DomainEvent AppointmentEnded {
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
      Instant endAt
    }
    DomainEvent AppointmentSuspended {
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
    }
    DomainEvent AppointmentReinstated {
      - AppointmentId appointmentId
    }
    DomainEvent NationalBoardCreated {
      - NationalBoardId nationalBoardId
    }

    Flow AppointmentFlow {
      command Appoint [ initiated by "Team leader, board leader or global administrator" ] delegates to Appointment [ -> AppointmentActive ] emits event AppointmentMade
      command ReviseAppointment delegates to Appointment [ AppointmentActive -> AppointmentActive ] emits event AppointmentRevised
      command SuspendAppointment delegates to Appointment [ AppointmentActive -> AppointmentSuspended ] emits event AppointmentSuspended
      command ReinstateAppointment delegates to Appointment [ AppointmentSuspended -> AppointmentActive ] emits event AppointmentReinstated
      command EndAppointment delegates to Appointment [ AppointmentActive, AppointmentSuspended -> AppointmentEnded* ] emits event AppointmentEnded
      command CreateNationalBoard [ initiated by "Global administrator" ] emits event NationalBoardCreated
    }
  }

  Service AppointmentFactSource {
    "Organization's implementation of AccessControl's RelationshipFactPort: current, nonsuspended appointments of active units in active departments. An appointment yields the role type that its position maps to: team member or team leader with team reach, board leader or board member with the board's reach. A current leadership of a local team also yields a derived board-member seat on its home department's board; a current leadership of a national team yields one on Hovedstyret. Both end with the leadership."
    boolean isTeamMember(PersonId person, TeamId team, Instant instant) : read-only;
    boolean isTeamLeader(PersonId person, TeamId team, Instant instant) : read-only;
    boolean boardLeaderCovers(PersonId person, DepartmentId department, Instant instant) : read-only;
    boolean isBoardMember(PersonId person, TeamId board, Instant instant) : read-only;
  }

  Service BoardMembership {
    "Derived, never stored: a department board's members are its appointed seats plus one derived seat for every current leader of a local team with its home in the department. Hovedstyret's members are its appointed seats plus one derived seat for every current leader of a national team. Mailing, group synchronization and the quorum rule read it."
    List<PersonId> boardMembers(TeamId board, Instant instant) : read-only;
    boolean nationalBoardQuorate(Instant instant) : read-only;
  }

  Service MembershipRegister {
    "Derived, never stored: a member is a student who holds an assistant, team or elected role, or who holds a granted membership for the calendar year. Membership lapses after three semesters without a role. An active member holds an assistant, team or board role in the current semester."
    boolean isMember(PersonId person, SemesterId semester) : read-only;
    boolean isActiveMember(PersonId person, SemesterId semester) : read-only;
  }
}

BoundedContext Schools implements PartnerSchools {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Partner-school identities, contacts, language, activity and department associations, and capacity plans per school, department and semester. There is no school deletion. Directory membership grants no maintenance authority."
  responsibilities = "Schools", "Department associations", "Capacity plans"

  "invariant: shared details require authority over every associated department; association changes require authority over the current and requested departments; a school without associations requires global authority. invariant: new schools and replacement association sets have at least one department. invariant: an association with dependent records (including saved placement proposals) cannot be removed."
  Aggregate School {
    Entity School {
      aggregateRoot
      - SchoolId schoolId
      String name
      - SchoolContact contact
      String language
      List<DepartmentId> associatedDepartments
      int revision
      - SchoolLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: schools.manage; requirement: global.administrator OR board.leader covering each requested department; scope: requested-departments; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void registerSchool(String name, List<DepartmentId> departments, String reason) : write [ -> SchoolActive ];
      "capability: schools.manage; requirement: covers every associated department; scope: school; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void reviseSchoolDetails(String name, @SchoolContact contact, String reason, int expectedRevision) : write [ SchoolActive -> SchoolActive ];
      "capability: schools.manage; requirement: covers current and requested departments; scope: school; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void replaceDepartmentAssociations(List<DepartmentId> departments, String reason, int expectedRevision) : write [ SchoolActive -> SchoolActive ];
      "Deactivation preserves capacity, placement, demand and history."
      def void deactivateSchool(String reason, int expectedRevision) : write [ SchoolActive -> SchoolInactive ];
      def void reactivateSchool(String reason, int expectedRevision) : write [ SchoolInactive -> SchoolActive ];
    }
    ValueObject SchoolId {
      int value key
    }
    "Contact details are data. A school contact is not a principal and holds no role; a coordinator records evidence that a contact supplies."
    ValueObject SchoolContact {
      String contactName
      ContactEmail emailAddress
      String phone
    }
    enum SchoolLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      SchoolActive, SchoolInactive
    }
  }

  "invariant: weekday counts are nonnegative; maintenance requires an active school, its department association and current authority for that department."
  Aggregate CapacityPlan {
    Entity CapacityPlan {
      aggregateRoot
      - CapacityPlanId capacityPlanId
      SchoolId schoolId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      SemesterId semesterId
      - WeekdayCounts counts
      int revision
      "capability: schools.capacity.manage; requirement: board.leader covering departmentId OR global.administrator; scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void setCapacity(@WeekdayCounts counts, String reason, int expectedRevision) : write;
    }
    ValueObject CapacityPlanId {
      int value key
    }
    ValueObject WeekdayCounts {
      int monday
      int tuesday
      int wednesday
      int thursday
      int friday
    }
  }
}

/* ======================================================================================
 * Volunteer recruitment
 * ====================================================================================== */

BoundedContext Admissions implements VolunteerRecruitment {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Admission periods per department and semester, public applications, and returning-assistant registrations. There is no inferred generic accepted-applicant fact."
  responsibilities = "Admission periods", "Applications", "Applicants", "Returning registrations"

  "invariant: one period per department and semester; the window is ordered and lies inside the semester. Openness is derived from the window and an instant."
  Aggregate AdmissionPeriod {
    Entity AdmissionPeriod {
      aggregateRoot
      - AdmissionPeriodId admissionPeriodId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      SemesterId semesterId
      Instant opensAt
      Instant closesAt
      int revision
      "capability: admissions.periods.manage; requirement: board.leader covering departmentId OR global.administrator; scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void defineAdmissionPeriod(DepartmentId departmentId, SemesterId semesterId, Instant opensAt, Instant closesAt) : write;
      def void reviseAdmissionPeriod(Instant opensAt, Instant closesAt, int expectedRevision) : write;
    }
    ValueObject AdmissionPeriodId {
      String value key
    }
  }

  Aggregate Applicant {
    "An applicant exists before a Person does; the account claim links it to a Person."
    Entity Applicant {
      aggregateRoot
      - ApplicantId applicantId
      ContactEmail normalizedEmail
      PersonId linkedPerson
    }
    ValueObject ApplicantId {
      String value key
    }
  }

  "invariant: one application per applicant and admission period. invariant: the field of study is active and belongs to the period's department. Admissions is the only writer of the year of study. invariant: the application states the applicant's weekday availability, bolk, and school wishes (level, school, language); the placement scheduling function reads them."
  Aggregate AdmissionApplication {
    Entity AdmissionApplication {
      aggregateRoot
      - ApplicationId applicationId
      ApplicantId applicantId
      AdmissionPeriodId admissionPeriodId
      FieldOfStudyId fieldOfStudyId
      int yearOfStudy
      String weekdayAvailability
      String bolkAvailability
      String schoolWishes
      String answers
      Instant submittedAt
      int revision
      - ApplicationLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: public; the anonymous submitter is rate limited by transport"
      def void submitApplication(ApplicantId applicantId, AdmissionPeriodId admissionPeriodId, int yearOfStudy) : write [ -> ApplicationSubmitted ];
      "capability: admissions.applications.revise; requirement: the applicant's linked Person (returning registration); a correction path for department managers, if kept, has its own specification; scope: own application; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void reviseYearOfStudy(int yearOfStudy, int expectedRevision) : write [ ApplicationSubmitted -> ApplicationSubmitted ];
      "capability: admissions.outcomes.announce; requirement: coordinator(department); scope: application-department; decisionTime: Transaction. A Ja recommendation derives Admitted with a placement or Substitute without one, on call; a Nei recommendation derives Rejected. School coordination announces the outcome after allocation."
      def void announceOutcome(@AdmissionOutcome outcome, int expectedRevision) : write [ ApplicationSubmitted -> OutcomeAnnounced ];
      "capability: admissions.outcomes.decide; requirement: board.leader covering departmentId, delegated to the recruitment team; scope: application-department; decisionTime: Transaction. A Kanskje recommendation implies no outcome: the recruitment team decides placed, substitute or rejected."
      def void decideOutcome(@AdmissionOutcome outcome, int expectedRevision) : write [ ApplicationSubmitted -> ApplicationSubmitted ];
    }
    ValueObject ApplicationId {
      String value key
    }
    enum AdmissionOutcome {
      Admitted, Substitute, Rejected
    }
    enum ApplicationLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ApplicationSubmitted, OutcomeAnnounced
    }
  }

  "invariant: registration requires accepted service history for the person; revisions are append-only."
  Aggregate ReturningRegistration {
    Entity ReturningRegistration {
      aggregateRoot
      - ReturningRegistrationId returningRegistrationId
      PersonId personId
      AdmissionPeriodId admissionPeriodId
      String preferences
      int revision
      "capability: admissions.returning.register; requirement: self with accepted history; scope: own person; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void registerReturning(AdmissionPeriodId admissionPeriodId, String preferences, int expectedRevision) : write;
    }
    ValueObject ReturningRegistrationId {
      String value key
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext Recruitment implements VolunteerRecruitment {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Interview staffing, scheduling, invitations and responses, conduct, recommendation, corrections and onboarding invitations. Recommendation, invitation, account claim, affiliation and placement stay separate decisions."
  responsibilities = "Interviews", "Questionnaires", "Onboarding invitations"

  "invariant: primary and co-interviewer are eligible, distinct people and neither is the linked applicant. invariant: completed or cancelled interviews reject staffing changes. invariant: an explicit recommendation is required to complete. invariant: each assigned interview keeps its saved questions; questionnaire changes affect future assignments only. invariant: a replacement schedule supersedes the previous invitation and resets the response to Pending; old links cannot reach the replacement."
  Aggregate Interview {
    Entity Interview {
      aggregateRoot
      - InterviewId interviewId
      ApplicationId applicationId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      PersonId interviewer
      PersonId coInterviewer
      - InterviewInvitation currentInvitation
      String questionSnapshot
      String recommendation
      int revision
      - InterviewLifecycle lifecycle

      "capability: recruitment.interviews.assign; requirement: board.leader covering departmentId; scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void assignApplicant(ApplicationId applicationId, PersonId interviewer) : write [ -> InterviewAssigned ];
      "capability: recruitment.staffing.manage; requirement: board.leader covering departmentId OR global.administrator; scope: interview; decisionTime: Transaction. Sends no new invitation."
      def void changeStaffing(PersonId interviewer, PersonId coInterviewer, String reason, int expectedRevision) : write;
      "capability: recruitment.interviews.schedule; requirement: the interviewer with requirement recruitment.interviewer-appointment, OR board.leader covering departmentId; scope: interview; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void scheduleInterview(Instant startsAt, String location) : write [ InterviewAssigned -> InterviewScheduled ];
      "Only after the applicant requested a new time; a replacement creates a new schedule and invitation."
      def void replaceSchedule(Instant startsAt, String location, int expectedRevision) : write [ InterviewScheduled -> InterviewScheduled ];
      "capability: bearer invitation link; only the current invitation accepts a response"
      def void respondToInvitation(String capability, String response) : write [ InterviewScheduled -> InterviewScheduled ];
      "capability: recruitment.interviews.conduct; requirement: interview.participant; scope: interview; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void completeInterview(String assessment, String recommendation) : write [ InterviewScheduled -> InterviewCompleted ];
      "A distinct no-show outcome with evidence, then rebook or close."
      def void recordNoShow(String evidence) : write [ InterviewScheduled -> InterviewNoShow ];
      def void rebookAfterNoShow(Instant startsAt, String location) : write [ InterviewNoShow -> InterviewScheduled ];
      def void cancelInterview(String reason) : write [ InterviewAssigned, InterviewScheduled, InterviewNoShow -> InterviewCancelled* ];
      "capability: recruitment.interviews.correct; requirement: interview.participant with requirement recruitment.correction-window; scope: interview; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void correctAssessment(String assessment, String recommendation, int expectedRevision) : write [ InterviewCompleted -> InterviewCompleted ];
    }
    ValueObject InterviewId {
      String value key
    }
    Entity InterviewInvitation {
      - InvitationId invitationId
      String capabilityDigest
      Instant startsAt
      String responseState
      Instant supersededAt
    }
    ValueObject InvitationId {
      String value key
    }
    enum InterviewLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      InterviewAssigned, InterviewScheduled, InterviewNoShow, InterviewCompleted, InterviewCancelled
    }
  }

  Aggregate Questionnaire {
    Entity Questionnaire {
      aggregateRoot
      - QuestionnaireId questionnaireId
      String questions
      int revision
      - QuestionnaireLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: recruitment.questionnaires.manage; requirement: global.administrator; scope: global; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void createQuestionnaire(String questions, String reason) : write [ -> QuestionnaireInactive ];
      def void reviseQuestionnaire(String questions, String reason, int expectedRevision) : write;
      def void activateQuestionnaire(String reason, int expectedRevision) : write [ QuestionnaireInactive -> QuestionnaireActive ];
      def void deactivateQuestionnaire(String reason, int expectedRevision) : write [ QuestionnaireActive -> QuestionnaireInactive ];
    }
    ValueObject QuestionnaireId {
      String value key
    }
    enum QuestionnaireLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      QuestionnaireActive, QuestionnaireInactive
    }
  }

  "Recruitment owns the invitation; Identity owns the account claim it requests. The invitation becomes Claimed when Identity reports the claim consumed, not through a shared row."
  Aggregate OnboardingInvitation {
    Entity OnboardingInvitation {
      aggregateRoot
      - OnboardingInvitationId onboardingInvitationId
      ApplicantId applicantId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      String claimCapabilityId
      - OnboardingInvitationLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: recruitment.onboarding.invite; requirement: board.leader covering departmentId; scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction. Reissue revokes the open invitation."
      def void issueInvitation(ApplicantId applicantId) : write [ -> InvitationIssued ];
      def void revokeInvitation() : write [ InvitationIssued -> InvitationRevoked* ];
      def void markInvitationClaimed() : write [ InvitationIssued -> InvitationClaimed* ];
    }
    ValueObject OnboardingInvitationId {
      String value key
    }
    enum OnboardingInvitationLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      InvitationIssued, InvitationRevoked, InvitationClaimed
    }
  }
}

/* ======================================================================================
 * School service (core)
 * ====================================================================================== */

BoundedContext Placements implements SchoolService {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Assistant supply (affiliation), semester placements, school demand, automatically drafted and reviewed proposals, confirmed rosters, dated school-service commitments, absences with a record of who covered each lesson date, days served and certificates, and immutable service outcomes and history. Substitutes and assistants arrange cover in Slack; the system records the result."
  responsibilities = "Volunteer affiliation", "Placements", "Demand", "Placement drafts, proposals and rosters", "Commitments", "Absence and coverage", "Days served and certificates", "Service history"
  implementationTechnology = "packages/domain/src/placements: portable contracts; packages/database/src/placements: PostgreSQL service Layer and adapters"

  Aggregate VolunteerAffiliation {
    Entity VolunteerAffiliation {
      aggregateRoot
      - AffiliationId affiliationId
      PersonId personId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      int revision
      - AffiliationLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: self; requirement: linked Person identity"
      def void requestAffiliation(DepartmentId departmentId) : write [ -> AffiliationPending ];
      "capability: placements.affiliations.establish; requirement: board.leader covering departmentId; scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void establishAffiliation(int expectedRevision) : write [ AffiliationPending -> AffiliationActive ];
      def void deactivateAffiliation(int expectedRevision) : write [ AffiliationActive -> AffiliationInactive ];
      def void reactivateAffiliation(int expectedRevision) : write [ AffiliationInactive -> AffiliationActive ];
    }
    ValueObject AffiliationId {
      String value key
    }
    enum AffiliationLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      AffiliationPending, AffiliationActive, AffiliationInactive
    }
  }

  "invariant: a placement requires an active affiliation in the school's associated department. invariant: placement history survives edits and removal; proposal generation never changes a placement."
  Aggregate Placement {
    Entity Placement {
      aggregateRoot
      - PlacementId placementId
      AffiliationId affiliationId
      SchoolId schoolId
      SemesterId semesterId
      - Weekday weekday
      String teachingBlock
      int revision
      - PlacementLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: placements.manage; requirement: coordinator(department) OR global.administrator; scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void placeAssistant(AffiliationId affiliationId, SchoolId schoolId, SemesterId semesterId) : write [ -> Placed ];
      def void revisePlacement(int expectedRevision) : write [ Placed -> Placed ];
      def void removePlacement(int expectedRevision) : write [ Placed -> PlacementRemoved* ];
      "capability: placements.own.read; requirement: placed assistant (self); scope: own placement; decisionTime: SnapshotRead. Assistants sign in to read their placement, receipts and profile."
      def @Placement readOwnPlacement() : read-only;
    }
    ValueObject PlacementId {
      String value key
    }
    enum Weekday {
      Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday
    }
    enum PlacementLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      Placed, PlacementRemoved
    }
  }

  Aggregate PlacementDemand {
    Entity PlacementDemand {
      aggregateRoot
      - DemandId demandId
      SchoolId schoolId
      SemesterId semesterId
      String weekday
      String teachingBlock
      int requiredVolunteers
      int revision
      "capability: placements.demand.manage; requirement: coordinator(department); scope: school-department; decisionTime: Transaction. The school is active."
      def void recordDemand(SchoolId schoolId, int requiredVolunteers) : write;
    }
    ValueObject DemandId {
      String value key
    }
  }

  "invariant: a proposal is an automated draft: a pure scheduling function assigns affiliated assistants to school demand from their weekday availability and bolk, within school capacity, and snapshots its inputs; every mismatch is explicit. Skolekoordinering adjusts the draft; confirmation requires an exact review of the remaining exceptions and freezes the roster."
  Aggregate PlacementProposal {
    Entity PlacementProposal {
      aggregateRoot
      - ProposalId proposalId
      DemandId demandId
      String rosterSnapshot
      String exceptions
      - ProposalLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: placements.proposals.draft; requirement: coordinator(department); scope: department-semester; decisionTime: Transaction. Runs the scheduling function; it drafts and never confirms."
      def void generateProposal(DemandId demandId) : write [ -> ProposalDrafted ];
      "capability: placements.proposals.draft; requirement: coordinator(department); scope: department-semester; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void adjustDraft(String assignments) : write [ ProposalDrafted -> ProposalDrafted ];
      "Queues one notification per assigned assistant; proves no dated service."
      def void confirmRoster(String reviewedExceptions) : write [ ProposalDrafted -> RosterConfirmed* ];
      def void discardProposal() : write [ ProposalDrafted -> ProposalDiscarded* ];
    }
    ValueObject ProposalId {
      String value key
    }
    Service PlacementScheduler {
      "A pure domain function, ported from the legacy scheduler: a greedy assignment improved by simulated annealing over weekday availability, bolk and school capacity. Same inputs give the same draft."
      String draftAssignments(String demand, String availability, String capacity) : read-only;
    }
    enum ProposalLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ProposalDrafted, RosterConfirmed, ProposalDiscarded
    }
  }

  "invariant: the interval starts before it ends and required demand is positive. invariant: Completed needs an immutable occurrence whose attendance, including recorded covering assistants, meets demand. invariant: a terminal decision is immutable and unique; concurrent or repeated commands cannot create a second one. Overdue is derived from the end time and an instant; time alone proves nothing."
  Aggregate SchoolServiceCommitment {
    Entity SchoolServiceCommitment {
      aggregateRoot
      - CommitmentId commitmentId
      SchoolId schoolId
      ProposalId confirmedRoster
      Instant startsAt
      Instant endsAt
      int requiredAssistants
      String scheduledAssignments
      - CommitmentLifecycle lifecycle

      "capability: placements.commitments.establish; requirement: coordinator(school, semester); scope: school-semester; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void establishCommitment(ProposalId confirmedRoster, Instant startsAt, Instant endsAt, int requiredAssistants) : write [ -> CommitmentOpen ];
      "capability: placements.commitments.decide; requirement: coordinator(school, semester); scope: commitment; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void recordCompletion(@ServiceOccurrence occurrence) : write [ CommitmentOpen -> CommitmentCompleted* ];
      def void recordCancellation(String reason, String source) : write [ CommitmentOpen -> CommitmentCancelled* ];
      def void recordUnfulfilled(String unmetDemand, String evidence) : write [ CommitmentOpen -> CommitmentUnfulfilled* ];
    }
    ValueObject CommitmentId {
      String value key
    }
    "Attendance lists only the people recorded as present; empty attendance is explicit."
    Entity ServiceOccurrence {
      - OccurrenceId occurrenceId
      String attendance
      Instant recordedAt
    }
    ValueObject OccurrenceId {
      String value key
    }
    enum CommitmentLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      CommitmentOpen, CommitmentCompleted, CommitmentCancelled, CommitmentUnfulfilled
    }
  }

  "invariant: an absence affects one scheduled assignment and stores no medical reason or free text; it does not erase the placement or the school's need. invariant: a coverage record names who covered one lesson date of the absence: a substitute on call (an admitted applicant without a placement) or another assistant. It is a recorded fact, not an offer."
  Aggregate Absence {
    Entity Absence {
      aggregateRoot
      - AbsenceId absenceId
      CommitmentId commitmentId
      PersonId absentAssistant
      - List<CoverageRecord> coverage
      - AbsenceLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: placements.absence.report; requirement: roster member (self) OR coordinator(school, semester); scope: commitment; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void reportAbsence(CommitmentId commitmentId, PersonId absentAssistant) : write [ -> AbsenceReported ];
      "capability: placements.coverage.record; requirement: roster member (self, for their own absence) OR coordinator(school, semester); scope: commitment; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void recordCoverage(String lessonDate, PersonId coveringAssistant) : write [ AbsenceReported -> AbsenceReported ];
      def void closeAbsence(CommitmentId occurrenceCommitment) : write [ AbsenceReported -> AbsenceCovered* X AbsenceUncovered* ];
    }
    ValueObject AbsenceId {
      String value key
    }
    ValueObject CoverageRecord {
      String lessonDate
      PersonId coveringAssistant
      Instant recordedAt
    }
    enum AbsenceLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      AbsenceReported, AbsenceCovered, AbsenceUncovered
    }
  }

  "invariant: days served are kept per assistant, department and semester; school coordination adjusts them at semester end, and each adjustment is attributable."
  Aggregate DaysServed {
    Entity SemesterService {
      aggregateRoot
      PersonId assistant
      DepartmentId departmentId
      SemesterId semesterId
      int daysServed
      int revision
      "capability: placements.days-served.adjust; requirement: coordinator(department); scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void adjustDaysServed(int daysServed, int expectedRevision) : write;
    }
  }

  "invariant: a certificate states the assistant, the department, the semesters and the days served from the recorded service; issuing a certificate never changes that record."
  Aggregate Certificate {
    Entity Certificate {
      aggregateRoot
      - CertificateId certificateId
      PersonId assistant
      DepartmentId departmentId
      SemesterId semesterId
      int daysServed
      Instant issuedAt
      "capability: certificates.issue; requirement: department.board covering departmentId OR a Hovedstyret seat when the department is not independent OR global.administrator; scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void issueCertificate(PersonId assistant, SemesterId semesterId) : write;
    }
    ValueObject CertificateId {
      String value key
    }
  }

  "invariant: append-only; importing history never creates a current affiliation, placement, demand, absence, occurrence, account or admission decision."
  Aggregate HistoricalService {
    Entity HistoricalServiceRecord {
      aggregateRoot
      String sourceIdentity
      PersonId personId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      SemesterId semesterId
      SchoolId schoolId
    }
  }

  Service DependentRecordQuery {
    "Placements' answer to Schools: does a school-department association have dependent records, including saved proposals?"
    boolean associationInUse(SchoolId schoolId, DepartmentId departmentId) : read-only;
  }
}

/* ======================================================================================
 * Economy and file custody
 * ====================================================================================== */

BoundedContext Economy implements ExpenseReimbursement {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Expense claims with private receipt files, approval, rejection and reopening, from assistants (travel to school) and team members (social events). Every member of the national economy team approves or rejects claims through a national delegation. Only its leader, the finance lead, pays out and records immutable settlement evidence, through a leaders-only delegation. Claim state, file custody, payment destinations, approval authority, settlement authority, delivery attempts and settlement history are separate facts."
  responsibilities = "Expense claims", "Payment destinations", "Settlement evidence"

  "invariant: approval does not prove payment and leaves the claim Approved. invariant: only pending claims can be revised, withdrawn, approved or rejected."
  Aggregate ExpenseClaim {
    Entity ExpenseClaim {
      aggregateRoot
      - ClaimId claimId
      PersonId claimant
      DepartmentId departmentId
      - Money amount
      String receiptFileRef
      String paymentAccountCiphertext
      int revision
      - ClaimLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: economy.claims.submit; requirement: self with an active payment-authority grant for departmentId; scope: own claim; decisionTime: Transaction. The claim keeps the ciphertext of the destination it was submitted against."
      def void submitClaim(@Money amount, String receiptFileRef) : write [ -> ClaimPending ];
      def void revisePendingClaim(@Money amount, int expectedRevision) : write [ ClaimPending -> ClaimPending ];
      def void withdrawPendingClaim(int expectedRevision) : write [ ClaimPending -> ClaimWithdrawn* ];
      "capability: economy.claims.approve; requirement: an active delegation of economy.claims.approve whose area covers departmentId, to a team on which the person holds a current appointment (the national delegation to every member of the economy team); scope: claim-department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void approveClaim(int expectedRevision) : write [ ClaimPending -> ClaimApproved ];
      def void rejectClaim(String reason, int expectedRevision) : write [ ClaimPending -> ClaimRejected ];
      def void reopenRejectedClaim(int expectedRevision) : write [ ClaimRejected -> ClaimPending ];
    }
    ValueObject ClaimId {
      String value key
    }
    ValueObject Money {
      int amountOre
      String currency
    }
    enum ClaimLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ClaimPending, ClaimApproved, ClaimRejected, ClaimWithdrawn
    }
  }

  "A payment destination is Economy-private data keyed by one payment-authority grant, recorded in the same transaction as the grant. The grant in AccessControl carries no private data."
  Aggregate PaymentDestination {
    Entity PaymentDestination {
      aggregateRoot
      GrantId paymentAuthorityGrantId key
      String paymentAccountCiphertext
      int revision
    }
  }

  "invariant: one settlement per claim; the claim is Approved at the observed revision; settledAt <= recordedAt; an external reference is unique per external authority; evidence is immutable."
  Aggregate Settlement {
    Entity SettlementEvidence {
      aggregateRoot
      - SettlementId settlementId
      ClaimId claimId
      int claimRevision
      int amountOre
      String destinationFingerprint
      String externalAuthority
      String externalReference
      Instant settledAt
      Instant recordedAt
      PersonId recordedBy
      "capability: economy.claims.settle; requirement: an active leaders-only delegation of economy.claims.settle whose area covers the claim department, to a team that the person currently leads (the finance lead of the economy team); scope: claim-department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void recordSettlement(ClaimId claimId, int claimRevision, String externalReference, Instant settledAt) : write;
    }
    ValueObject SettlementId {
      String value key
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext FileCustody implements FileCustodyDomain {
  type = SYSTEM
  domainVisionStatement = "Private files with no-follow traversal, ownership checks, restricted permissions and explicit lifecycle. A path string is not authority."
  responsibilities = "Private files"

  Aggregate PrivateFile {
    Entity PrivateFile {
      aggregateRoot
      - PrivateFileId privateFileId
      String owningFact
      String sha256
      - FileLifecycle lifecycle
      def void stageFile(String sha256) : write [ -> FileStaged ];
      def void promoteFile() : write [ FileStaged -> FileCommitted ];
      def void deleteFile() : write [ FileStaged, FileCommitted -> FileDeleted* ];
    }
    ValueObject PrivateFileId {
      String value key
    }
    enum FileLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      FileStaged, FileCommitted, FileDeleted
    }
  }
}

/* ======================================================================================
 * Supporting contexts
 * ====================================================================================== */

BoundedContext TeamApplications implements TeamRecruitment {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "A visitor applies to one team. Team members read the team's applications; the current team leader changes intake and deletes applications. Global administration grants no implicit access. No review outcome, hiring state or appointment."
  responsibilities = "Team applications", "Team intake"

  "invariant: a submission stores one application with its submission instant; exact replay returns the original result; a distinct submission is a second application. invariant: deletion removes the application and its private fields from every stored notification. invariant: audit records no applicant contact details or free text. Applications are purged after a fixed retention period (period to be set)."
  Aggregate TeamApplication {
    Entity TeamApplication {
      aggregateRoot
      - TeamApplicationId teamApplicationId
      TeamId teamId
      - ApplicantDetails details
      Instant submittedAt
      - TeamApplicationLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: public; the anonymous submitter is rate limited by transport; guard: the team's intake is Open at the Clock instant"
      def void submitTeamApplication(TeamId teamId, @ApplicantDetails details) : write [ -> ApplicationStored ];
      "capability: team-applications.manage; requirement: team.leader(teamId), current and nonsuspended; scope: team-of(application); decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void deleteTeamApplication() : write [ ApplicationStored -> ApplicationDeleted* ];
      "Purges the application after the fixed retention period (period to be set)."
      def void purgeTeamApplication() : write [ ApplicationStored -> ApplicationPurged* ];
    }
    ValueObject TeamApplicationId {
      String value key
    }
    ValueObject ApplicantDetails {
      String name
      ContactEmail emailAddress
      String phone
      String yearOfStudy
      String fieldOfStudy
      String biography
      String motivation
    }
    enum TeamApplicationLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ApplicationStored, ApplicationDeleted, ApplicationPurged
    }
  }

  "TeamApplications owns the intake with its own revision; the intake is not stored on Organization's team row. invariant: the intake revision belongs to the intake, not to the Organization team. Open is derived: team and department active, intake accepts applications, deadline absent or later than now (the deadline instant is closed), and a deliverable mailbox exists (team email, else department email; an undeliverable team email does not fall back)."
  Aggregate TeamIntake {
    Entity TeamIntake {
      aggregateRoot
      TeamId teamId
      boolean acceptApplication
      Instant deadline
      int revision
      "capability: team-applications.manage; requirement: team.leader(teamId), current and nonsuspended; scope: team; decisionTime: Transaction; precondition: observed revision"
      def void reviseIntake(boolean acceptApplication, Instant deadline, int expectedRevision) : write;
    }
    Service TeamIntakePolicy {
      String evaluateIntake(String teamIntakeFacts, Instant now) : read-only;
    }
  }

  Application TeamApplicationsApplication {
    "capability: public; rate limited"
    Command SubmitTeamApplication {
      String commandId
      TeamId teamId
      - ApplicantDetails details
    }
    "capability: team-applications.manage; requirement: team.leader; scope: team-of(application); decisionTime: Transaction"
    Command DeleteTeamApplication {
      String commandId
      - TeamApplicationId teamApplicationId
    }
    "capability: team-applications.manage; requirement: team.leader; scope: team; decisionTime: Transaction"
    Command ReviseTeamIntake {
      String commandId
      TeamId teamId
      boolean acceptApplication
      Instant deadline
    }
    Command QueueApplicantReceipt
    Command QueueTeamNotification
    Command CancelTeamApplicationEnvelopes

    DomainEvent TeamApplicationSubmitted {
      - TeamApplicationId teamApplicationId
      TeamId teamId
      Instant submittedAt
    }
    DomainEvent TeamApplicationDeleted {
      - TeamApplicationId teamApplicationId
      TeamId teamId
    }
    DomainEvent TeamIntakeRevised {
      TeamId teamId
      boolean acceptApplication
      Instant deadline
      int revision
    }
    // Applications are purged after a fixed retention period (period to be set).
    DomainEvent TeamApplicationPurged {
      - TeamApplicationId teamApplicationId
      TeamId teamId
      String retentionPolicy
    }

    Flow TeamApplicationFlow {
      command SubmitTeamApplication [ initiated by "Visitor" ] delegates to TeamApplication [ -> ApplicationStored ] emits event TeamApplicationSubmitted
      event TeamApplicationSubmitted triggers command QueueApplicantReceipt + QueueTeamNotification
      command DeleteTeamApplication [ initiated by "Team leader" ] delegates to TeamApplication [ ApplicationStored -> ApplicationDeleted* ] emits event TeamApplicationDeleted
      event TeamApplicationDeleted triggers command CancelTeamApplicationEnvelopes
      command ReviseTeamIntake [ initiated by "Team leader" ] emits event TeamIntakeRevised
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext SocialEvents implements CommunityLife {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Social events for student members of a department in a semester."
  responsibilities = "Social events"

  Aggregate SocialEvent {
    Entity SocialEvent {
      aggregateRoot
      - SocialEventId socialEventId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      SemesterId semesterId
      String audience
      String title
      Instant startsAt
      Instant endsAt
      "capability: social-events.create; requirement: department member with the event grant; scope: department; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void announceEvent(DepartmentId departmentId, SemesterId semesterId, String title, Instant startsAt, Instant endsAt) : write;
    }
    ValueObject SocialEventId {
      String value key
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext Content implements PublicPresence {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Public articles with drafts and published versions, public page text and sponsor presentation. Bodies are sanitized; slugs are unique."
  responsibilities = "Articles", "Page text", "Sponsors"

  Aggregate Article {
    Entity Article {
      aggregateRoot
      - ArticleId articleId
      String slug
      String draftBody
      int publishedVersion
      int revision
      - ArticleLifecycle lifecycle
      "capability: content.articles.edit; requirement: editor in an active department; scope: article-departments; decisionTime: Transaction"
      def void createDraft(String title, String body) : write [ -> ArticleDraft ];
      def void reviseDraft(String body, int expectedRevision) : write;
      "capability: content.articles.publish; requirement: publisher; a leader may not publish organization-wide articles"
      def void publishArticle(int expectedRevision) : write [ ArticleDraft, ArticleUnpublished -> ArticlePublished ];
      def void unpublishArticle(int expectedRevision) : write [ ArticlePublished -> ArticleUnpublished ];
    }
    ValueObject ArticleId {
      int value key
    }
    enum ArticleLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ArticleDraft, ArticlePublished, ArticleUnpublished
    }
  }

  Aggregate PageText {
    Entity PageText {
      aggregateRoot
      String pageKey
      String body
      int revision
      def void revisePageText(String body, int expectedRevision) : write;
    }
  }

  Aggregate SponsorPresentation {
    Entity Sponsor {
      aggregateRoot
      String sponsorKey
      String name
      String logoRef
      int revision
      def void reviseSponsor(String name, String logoRef, int expectedRevision) : write;
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext Contact implements PublicPresence {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Relays a visitor's contact message to an active department mailbox. The message is transient; only the quota is durable. Submission is anonymous and rate limited per visitor address. The homepage server authenticates to the backend with a deployment secret; that secret names no principal."
  responsibilities = "Contact quota", "Contact relay"

  "invariant: at most a fixed number of attempts per visitor address per rolling window; the attempt is consumed before recipient lookup or delivery and is never refunded."
  Aggregate ContactQuota {
    Entity ContactQuota {
      aggregateRoot
      String visitorAddress
      Instant windowStart
      int attempts
      def void consumeAttempt(Instant now) : write;
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext Mailing implements Outreach {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Mailing recipients for a department, semester and cohort (assistants, team members, union), native list administration and automated Google Workspace synchronization. The first synchronization scope keeps team group membership, derived Styret seats included, in sync with team membership; accounts stay manual. Reads do not administer subscriptions or send mail."
  responsibilities = "Recipient projection", "Mailing lists", "Workspace synchronization"

  Aggregate MailingList {
    Entity MailingList {
      aggregateRoot
      - MailingListId mailingListId
      DepartmentId departmentId
      String cohort
      String workspaceGroup
      - MailingListLifecycle lifecycle
      def void defineList(DepartmentId departmentId, String cohort) : write [ -> ListActive ];
      def void retireList() : write [ ListActive -> ListRetired* ];
      def void synchronizeWorkspace() : write;
    }
    ValueObject MailingListId {
      String value key
    }
    enum MailingListLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      ListActive, ListRetired
    }
  }

  Service RecipientProjection {
    "Current authority and recipient facts share one read snapshot. An explicit semester must exist; an omitted semester resolves to the unique current one. capability: mailing.recipients.read; requirement: board.leader covering departmentId OR global.administrator (every department); decisionTime: SnapshotRead"
    String recipients(DepartmentId departmentId, SemesterId semesterId, String cohort) : read-only;
  }
}

BoundedContext Messaging implements Outreach {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Admission-opening notices with subscription consent and unsubscribe, accept-interview reminders and staff interview digests. Email only."
  responsibilities = "Notice subscriptions", "Reminders", "Digests"

  Aggregate NoticeSubscription {
    Entity NoticeSubscription {
      aggregateRoot
      - SubscriptionId subscriptionId
      ContactEmail emailAddress
      DepartmentId departmentId
      - SubscriptionLifecycle lifecycle
      def void subscribeToNotices(ContactEmail emailAddress, DepartmentId departmentId) : write [ -> Subscribed ];
      def void unsubscribeFromNotices(String unsubscribeToken) : write [ Subscribed -> Unsubscribed* ];
    }
    ValueObject SubscriptionId {
      String value key
    }
    enum SubscriptionLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      Subscribed, Unsubscribed
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext Delivery implements DurableDelivery {
  type = SYSTEM
  domainVisionStatement = "Every command that needs external work commits one immutable envelope with its business fact. Workers claim, attempt, acknowledge or retry after commit. Retry reuses the envelope and effect identity; a provider failure never rolls back the business fact."
  responsibilities = "Outbox envelopes", "Claims and fencing", "Retry and quarantine", "Mail port"

  "invariant: the first envelope is immutable. invariant: a claim is exclusive and fenced; a lost claim is a typed failure. invariant: an effect stays behind an undelivered predecessor of the same owner when ordering is declared. invariant: historical import never enqueues."
  Aggregate OutboxEnvelope {
    Entity OutboxEnvelope {
      aggregateRoot
      - EffectId effectId
      String owningContext
      String owningFact
      String payload
      int attempts
      - EnvelopeLifecycle lifecycle
      def void enqueue(String owningFact, String payload) : write [ -> EnvelopePending ];
      def void claim(String claimId) : write [ EnvelopePending -> EnvelopeClaimed ];
      def void acknowledge(String claimId) : write [ EnvelopeClaimed -> EnvelopeDelivered* ];
      def void failAttempt(String claimId) : write [ EnvelopeClaimed -> EnvelopePending ];
      def void quarantine(String claimId) : write [ EnvelopeClaimed -> EnvelopeQuarantined* ];
      "The owning context cancels undelivered work (for example a deleted team application) and clears the private payload."
      def void cancel() : write [ EnvelopePending, EnvelopeClaimed -> EnvelopeCancelled* ];
    }
    ValueObject EffectId {
      String value key
    }
    enum EnvelopeLifecycle {
      aggregateLifecycle
      EnvelopePending, EnvelopeClaimed, EnvelopeDelivered, EnvelopeQuarantined, EnvelopeCancelled
    }
  }
}

BoundedContext Reporting implements OperationalReporting {
  type = FEATURE
  domainVisionStatement = "Read models over owned facts: applicant progress, coordinator reports (an archive export at cutover; each report is built for a named consumer), and General Assembly vote weights. Reports accept no commands."
  responsibilities = "Applicant progress", "Coordinator reports", "General Assembly vote weights"

  Aggregate ApplicantProgressView {
    "Shows recorded facts in sequence (interview, invitation, claim, affiliation, placement); it never invents an admission answer."
    ValueObject ApplicantProgress {
      ApplicantId applicantId
      String stage
    }
    Service ApplicantProgressProjection {
      @ApplicantProgress progressOf(ApplicantId applicantId) : read-only;
    }
  }

  "Each department gets its active members plus 100 votes, split equally among its attending members, at most 25 votes per member. The quorum needs one representative from each independent department. The report derives the weights; the vote happens at the meeting."
  Aggregate GeneralAssemblyVoteWeights {
    ValueObject DepartmentVoteWeight {
      DepartmentId departmentId
      int activeMembers
      int attendingMembers
      int votesPerAttendingMember
    }
    Service VoteWeightProjection {
      @DepartmentVoteWeight weightFor(DepartmentId departmentId, SemesterId semesterId, int attendingMembers) : read-only;
    }
  }
}

